\subsection{\code{BaseRDotchartLayerProcessor$extract_data()}}{
  Read the dots out of the recorded \code{dotchart()} call.

\code{dotchart(x, labels = NULL, ...)} names its dots from \code{labels} when
the caller gives them and from \code{names(x)} otherwise, which is what the
chart draws down its left margin. A vector with neither is drawn
against blank labels, and is emitted here against its positions so a
reader still has something to navigate by.

\code{x} and \code{y} carry the magnitude and the category respectively, which
is the arrangement a \code{horz} layer means -- see the class note.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{BaseRDotchartLayerProcessor$extract_data(layer_info)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{layer_info}}{Information about the recorded plot call}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    List of \code{x}/\code{y} points, empty when there is nothing to read
  }
}

